{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And Moses sent.</b> A term of escort, as in 'and Abraham went with them לשלחם' (to send them off). One may say: the entire pericope, from 'and Jethro heard' until 'and he went to his land,' is after the giving of the Torah. And so the interpretation of 'and Jethro came' — on the tenth of Tishrei, on which Moses came down from the mountain — 'and Moses went out to meet his father-in-law' on that very day; 'and Moses told his father-in-law' etc. in sequence until 'and Aaron came and all the elders of Israel' — on that very day when he came down from the mountain it was. 'And it was on the next day' — the day after the feast, on which Moses came down from the mountain — was to teach Torah to Israel, as Rashi explained at the end of pericope Ki Tissa. 'And Moses sat to judge the people' etc. in sequence until 'and he did all that he said' — this is what is written in pericope Devarim: 'I am not able alone to bear you' etc. until 'and I made them heads over you, captains of thousands, captains of fifties, and captains of tens.' One may say Jethro remained there with Israel until the second year, when Moses said to him 'come with us' etc. And along with the thread of the Exodus from Egypt, with which it was occupied, it included pericope Yitro here, because it too begins and deals with the Exodus from Egypt; and even though it proceeds and continues with matters of Torah and laws, in order to connect it to pericope of the giving of the Torah, it interrupted the matter of Jethro thereby; and it cited as the conclusion of Jethro's matter, namely 'and Moses sent his father-in-law' etc. And according to this approach, Gershom and Eliezer must not have stood at Mount Sinai, even though there is no proof for this matter — there is a reminder of the matter, in that they were not mentioned from here onward in any place in the Torah."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:42.777441089Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}